     'Leopards on granite are lovely subjects, but they are often distant and move fast. The right kit and a few settings improve your odds.',
     [['The lens', 'A 100–400mm or 200–500mm telephoto covers most subjects, while a 70–200mm helps for close sightings and landscapes. On a crop-sensor camera, a 300mm already gives good reach.'],
